WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:07.120
Surprising news appeared - an artist spent a 100&nbsp;
hours creating something truly incredible for a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:14.640
book cover image…unfortunately, only to be accused&nbsp;
having used an AI. However, when I looked at this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:23.000
my first thought was that this looks way too&nbsp;
good for an AI image in 2023. Why is that? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:29.240
look. There is so much detail in this image,&nbsp;
no state of the art text to image AI system&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:37.000
can match it. The resolution of this image, the&nbsp;
number of pixels are just too high. Until now.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:41.480
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:46.920
Now, previous techniques already exist to&nbsp;
increase the resolution of input images,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:52.600
or even videos. This is what we&nbsp;
call upscaling or super resolution,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:59.920
and it is starting to appear in video games, and&nbsp;
in some cases, it already runs in real time. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:06.760
why not apply it to these AI-made photos,&nbsp;
that should be easier than video, right?

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:14.400
Well, not quite. You see, super resolution means&nbsp;
that we introduce new information into an image.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:21.040
And this new information is unfortunately, not&nbsp;
always what should be there. For instance, text&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:28.120
can easily get mangled in video games. If we have&nbsp;
a stationary photo that we would like to frame,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:36.520
it better not have artifacts like this, right?&nbsp;
So, is all hope lost for high-resolution images?

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:40.800
That was what I thought, until&nbsp;
I saw the news from Midjourney,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:47.680
a popular text to image AI system, which can&nbsp;
now create incredibly detailed, high-resolution&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:54.880
images with a recent update. And the results&nbsp;
are truly insane. How does it work? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.880 --> 00:02:01.440
you first generate a lower resolution image,&nbsp;
these are pretty good, however, when we start&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:07.800
zooming in, we start to see the limits of this&nbsp;
resolution. But then, hold on to your papers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:18.040
because we can ask it to perform 4x super&nbsp;
resolution, and then, this happens. There is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:25.440
just so much more detail in these images, I am&nbsp;
completely stunned. Wow. This seems like years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:31.920
and years of progress, and it just dropped a few&nbsp;
days ago in an update like nothing had happened.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:37.800
Now, other super resolution or image&nbsp;
upscaling systems also exist. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:43.360
they are in abundance today. We have&nbsp;
so many options. However, this kind of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:50.000
quality is beyond what I have seen from other&nbsp;
solutions out there. According to other users,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:57.400
it is perhaps matched only by the Gigapixel&nbsp;
AI system, I gave it a brief try and did not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:03.880
have too much luck with it so far. It is also a&nbsp;
standalone application, which is not necessary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:12.200
when it is built right into the text to image AI.&nbsp;
For me, so far, this workflow has been unmatched.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:15.960
And it just delivers over and over again.

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:20.840
My opinion is that these techniques&nbsp;
are deceivingly useful. You see,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:26.720
you may often have an image that is a&nbsp;
regular photograph or an AI-generated work,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:33.720
where you love the image, but the framing is not&nbsp;
quite perfect, and you would only like to use&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:40.320
one small part of it. However, when you do that,&nbsp;
you take the parts that you like, and suddenly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:46.680
there are just not enough details for this&nbsp;
image to stand on its own. And in these cases,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:52.640
these super resolution techniques can&nbsp;
make or break that image. Loving it.

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:59.280
Now, not even this new technique is perfect, not&nbsp;
even close. In some cases, excessive smoothing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:06.360
happens, which is quite curious. Look. You would&nbsp;
think that this is the low resolution image,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:11.720
and this is the upscaled, but that is&nbsp;
not the case. Due to this smoothing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:19.640
details are not only not added to the image,&nbsp;
but some can even disappear in the process! But,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:24.760
in return, the overall image and the&nbsp;
edges of the objects are way sharper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:29.240
so there are cases where this is a&nbsp;
trade off that we have to consider.

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:33.960
And, my goodness, through the&nbsp;
power of AI research, today,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:40.720
everyone can experience the amazing feeling of&nbsp;
their artistic ideas coming to life. There are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:47.520
already systems that even work on the phone&nbsp;
in your pocket. Wow. And to think that text&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:55.240
to video also exists, just imagine that soon,&nbsp;
this is what will happen to videos too. Soon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.240 --> 00:05:00.600
everyone will be able to become a movie&nbsp;
director, first, for at a small cost,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:07.280
and then, over time, all this will be free&nbsp;
for all of us. What a time to be alive!

